The AD&D game after which all these dungeon crawls are modeled makes those
little "."'s ten by ten foot squares.  Keep that in mind, and a lot of things
suddenly become more intuitive.  For example, you are not really standing
_on_ the chest, just within ten feet of it.  I grant you, translating the
"." _direction_ as "down" doesn't help the intuition much.  ;-)  A better
intuition would be to translate "." as "pointing at the contents of this
square."

[Of course, if the game ever allowed you to polymorph yourself into a gibbon
of gigantic size, reaching that chest in the next square might not be so
silly! And a gibbon has plenty of dexterity for picking locks.  Hint to
